[#:seon.task{:name "preserve-primary-and-suppressed-causes"
             :kind :function
             :intent "One normalization keeps every cause link once (a cause cycle ends at its first repeat) and the chains of suppressed throwables, so a cleanup failure kept by .addSuppressed survives beside the primary (audit §2.2)."
             :must-read #{seon.error.refusal/chain seon.error.refusal/root-frame}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/error-delivery-audit-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "errors-reference-worlds-never-copy-them"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An error holds references, never copies (owner 2026-09-26: \"not the entire database\"): a database, connection, projection, environment or SCI context in an error's members or any cause link's ex-data is its registry-declared identity, and an over-bound value is its size. Measured before: three real refusals each printed over 20 MB (a projection prints over 2 GB)."
             :must-read #{seon.error.refusal/references seon.error.refusal/diagnostic seon.error.refusal/chain}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/err-refs-sweep-opus-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "refusal-offending-arguments-held-by-reference"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An invalid-input refusal carries the offending arguments as values in its ex-data (:seon.error/offending [unit]); anything that prints or stores the diagnostic can realize them — a test failure pr-str'd an endless lazy seq and OOM'd default on 2026-09-27 (fixed at the runner in b703e5ae9 by storing through admission's bound, which still realizes up to 8 MiB). Hold offending arguments by reference (result handle / blob digest / bounded admitted value) at the producer so no consumer can realize more than what is shown."
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/large-value-feedback-opus-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-refusal-omits-the-data-that-explains-it"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A refusal reaches the agent as its message and a two-frame stack; the evidence its producer decided on is not in the value. Dogfood loop 2026-09-28: propose-merge! refused 'Cannot interpret seon.sci.eval/acquire-program!: ... calls a definition this branch changes' without naming which changed definition or the call path from the refused declaration to it; finding that (seon.render.value/tree, 419 transitive callers, 13 host-bound) took a second evaluation written by hand. A producer's refusal carries the data it decided on (here the changed definitions reached and one path to each), by reference when large, so the reply explains itself and no refusal needs digging."
             :must-read #{seon.error.refusal/diagnostic}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-loop-2026-09-28.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "hand-built-error-maps-remain-across-the-namespaces"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "Error sweep: batch 1 converted config (0a75ca319 detection only), the test runner (32ebd64f6) and cluster.agent (d0961f05e); hand-built error maps and per-namespace copies of the error helpers (error?, error, let-ok) remain: ai.clj:635, plan-era copies, render/transcript.clj:744, the 44 (contains? x :seon.error/at) checks, the 15 three-key checks and the 17 debt: comments (tmp/root-cause-census/report.md). Rule: every error is built by ONE constructor validated against its declared alternative where it is made. Done when each remaining namespace, one per commit, rewrites its error? ladders first, then literal maps grouped by enclosing defn with the alternative from its output union (boot-time producers checked: error refuses without a projection), and the census counts fall to zero for it."
             :must-read #{seon.error.refusal/error? seon.error/render-faults-ai}
             :evidence #{"tmp/root-cause-census/report.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "errors-capture-whole-stack-traces"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "Errors and caller lookups capture or walk whole stack traces: error.refusal stack-frames and current-frames, instrument caller-frame, schema fallback-caller, fs caller-frame and Throwable->map stored whole as :seon.error/cause or :seon.error/offending (test runner result-read-error, sci kernel triage, sci admit, operator launch forms). Owner 2026-10-07: 10k-line traces are useless; Seon's own error carries the producer's source location and the cause chain (class, message, ex-data per link) as data, never a trace. Inventory class stack-trace, 15 sites: error/refusal.clj 4, script/operator.clj 2, instrument.clj 2, schema.clj 2, script/operator_outcome_test.clj 1, fs.clj 1, sci/admit.clj 1, sci/kernel.clj 1, test/runner.clj 1. Done when no error value or stored fact holds a stack trace or Throwable->map, caller attribution reads one frame by StackWalker limit, and seon.error.refusal-test asserts a 5,000-deep recursion's error holds its chain and location with no frame list."
             :must-read #{seon.error.refusal/chain seon.instrument/caller-frame seon.schema/fallback-caller}
             :evidence #{"tmp/no-print-hash/print-sites.tsv" "tmp/no-print-hash/notes.md"}}]
